Stripe Test Mode result
- Checkout displayed and charged EUR 29.90 in Stripe Test Mode using the standard 4242 test card.
- Stripe recorded one Succeeded EUR 29.90 transaction for the synthetic deployment account.
- FitHub initially retained the payment as Pending when the old API transaction code failed under Neon retry execution strategy.
- Commit 942b61c made the complete database transaction the retry unit and was deployed before reconciliation was repeated.
- The existing paid Checkout session was reconciled; no second payment was created.
- FitHub payment history then showed Succeeded, EUR 29.90, and the Member reached /dashboard.
- Neon independently confirmed one payment row and an Active membership.
- Stripe's Event deliveries view showed successful deliveries to the deployed FitHub webhook.
- Membership activation remained based on server-side Stripe verification; the browser redirect alone did not activate it.

Password-reset email
- The hosted application uses the configured Brevo HTTPS provider and public frontend base URL.
- A hosted end-to-end reset email was not sent because no safe deliverable Phase 3 recipient was configured for the synthetic account during this run.
- Local Mailpit password-reset delivery, single-use completion and token-reuse rejection are covered by GAP-002-password-reset.log.
- Decision for hosted Brevo delivery: NOT TESTED.

Cold start and free-tier limitations
- Render warns that the free API instance may sleep after inactivity and can delay a request by 50 seconds or more.
- The Angular client and SignalR clients are configured to reconnect, but a full sleep-duration cold-start test was not performed in this run.
- Equipment fault photographs stored on the Render container filesystem are ephemeral; fault reports themselves remain persisted in Neon and photographs are optional.

Decision
- Public frontend, API health, Neon persistence/migrations, role login routing, simulator connectivity, Stripe Test payment, webhook delivery, payment persistence and membership activation: PASSED.
- Hosted Brevo delivery and a full free-tier sleep/wake cycle: NOT TESTED as described above.
- Overall deployment verification: PASSED WITH DOCUMENTED FREE-TIER AND EMAIL-DELIVERY LIMITATIONS.
